From 5aeff235f3666176eeafc9aa4456a4e801714b49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 4 <phase4@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 08:32:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] RISC-V: restrict WCH vendor extensions to the observed
 set

The official WCH 12.2 assembler rejects unknown X-prefixed extension names, with or without explicit versions, while accepting XW and the single-letter X extension. Add the bare X entry to the vendor table introduced earlier in this series, and use that table for recognition as well as for default-version lookup, so an unknown name is rejected instead of being accepted silently.

Retarget the inherited generic-vendor tests onto the accepted names and add exact diagnostics for the march, attribute and option paths. march-fail-single-prefix-x.d is deleted rather than retargeted: it asserted that a bare rv32ix fails, which is no longer true, and the other single-letter prefixes stay covered by march-fail-single-prefix.l.

WCH 12.2 behavior evidence: tmp/phase4-evidence/s1-official/diagnostics.tsv and the accept/reject matrix in tmp/phase4-evidence/vendor-x-calibration/, which records rv32ix, rv32ix1p0 and rv32ix9p9 as accepted and rv32imac_xq, rv32i_xargle and rv32i_xargle2p0 as rejected with the official diagnostic text.
